A Springer [[Amulet]] had been discovered by [[Eathon Lambert]] and used on his adventures. {{source|Huntik.com}} Eathon eventually hid Springer's Amulet in the [[Paris Catacombs]] with the intent of it being passed onto his son, [[Lok Lambert]]. The Amulet was hidden inside of a square puzzle that triggered a time-based trap, forcing Lok to solve the puzzle. During the time he spent solving it, he unknowingly bonded with Springer. {{source|Crawling the Catacombs}} Lok later summoned Springer for the first time to open a locked box inside the [[Paris Catacombs]]. {{source|Divide and Conquer}} 

Lok called on Springer in the [[Temple of Thor]] in order to untie the [[Gleipnir]] rope so that the Huntik Team could tie up and defeat a wild [[Fenris]]. {{source|Two Powers Become One}} 

Springer was used by Lok in conjunction with several other Titans to create a mechanism to bring a shipwreck they initially suspected was the [[Argo]] to the surface. {{Source|The Treasures of the Argonauts}} 

Lok invoked Springer in the [[Tomb of Nefertiti]] in order to activate a release mechanism to deactivate a sand trap Dante Vale was in. Dante invoked [[Solwing]] to fly Springer to the mechanism, and he was able to activate it before Dante was smothered by the sand. While in the chamber Dante was trapped in, Springer ended up finding a secret passage [[Eathon Lambert]] meant Lok to find. {{Source|The Sceptre Deception}} 

The Titan was called by Lok again to free the Huntik Team from a cage the [[Amazons]] put them in. Springer united the ropes [[Sophie Casterwill|Sophie]] and [[Cherit]] were trapped in. {{Source|Ladies' Choice}} 

Springer was invoked by Lok to handle the traps while they were going down the entrance of [[King Solomon's Mines]]. Dante and [[Tersly]] invoked their [[Red Searcher]] Titans to first spot the traps, but no trap was found for Springer to handle. {{Source|To Be Together}} 

In [[Tower of Nostradamus|Nostradamus' Tower]], Lok called Springer to untie [[Peter]] from the rope [[the Organization]] tied him with upon raiding the tower. {{Source|The Tower of Nostradamus}} 

During the mission at [[Klaus' bookshop]] to recover the Amulet of [[Void]], Springer was able to knock over a bookshelf and find the hidden elevator down to the lab. There, he assisted Lok in accessing the secret locker containing Void's Amulet and also helped to bite through and free the Huntik team from the vines of [[Dark Dryad]]. {{source|The Blood Spiral}}

Springer's amulet was briefly shown during Lok's dream induced by [[Arc]] as all of Lok's amulets were forced out of his bag and turned into [[Harlekin]] Titans. {{Source|The Legendary Titan of Fate}} 

Lok invoked Springer once again in the [[Pyramid of the Sun]] to search the room he was in. Springer managed to find and press two buttons that unlocked pyrotechnic material, later used by Lok to get access to the Legendary Titan of Summons, [[Quetzalcoatl]]. {{Source|The Titan in the Temple of Sun}}

At one point, Lok used Springer to deactivate a trap that would have squashed them. {{Source|TCG:SAS-071|SAS-071}}

At another undisclosed moment, Springer was invoked by Lok to sneak behind enemy lines. {{Source|TCG:LGS-039|LGS-039}}

[[File:S1E15 Springer springs the trap.jpg|thumb|Springer saves [[Dante Vale|Dante]]'s life by deactivating a sand trap's mechanism]]
Springer is a Titan skilled at solving complex puzzles and intricate traps. After he studies the trap and its workings, he is capable of pressing a glowing claw to it, and it magically pops open, deactivates, or harmlessly goes off. {{Source|Divide and Conquer}} {{Source|The Sceptre Deception}} This includes even untying complex knots, which he can either do manually by using his claws, {{Source|Two Powers Become One}} or simply wagging his tail on the knots. {{Source|Ladies' Choice}} His sharp teeth can be useful for biting through vines and ropes, and his claws allow him to climb virtually any surface. He is also quite quick on his feet {{Source|The Blood Spiral}} and very perceptive of things such as hidden passages. {{Source|The Sceptre Deception}} Springer can also be very effective at flanking enemy lines due to his sneaky nature. {{Source|TCG:LGS-039|LGS-039}}

